(6719920, 1004326, 109387, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RyanWareham:</b></div><hr/><i> After this shot I learned how to properly expose and shoot night scenery. <br/>Lighting on building was hard to adjust due to floodlights from work crews.... it looked better on camera screen so I was happy at the time.<br/>Think hdr could''ve helped this if I had shot some various exposure shots.... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You don''t necessarily need an HDR to achieve a good result. In this kind of shots it''s better to shoot during the blue hour after sunset when the equilibrium between light and darkness is perfect.<br/> <br/>Moreover here you could fix the distorsion of the buildings.</td>', 'Originally posted by RyanWareham: After this shot I learned how to properly expose and shoot night scenery. Lighting on building was hard to adjust due to floodlights from work crews.... it looked better on camera screen so I was happy at the time.Think hdr could''ve helped this if I had shot some various exposure shots....   You don''t necessarily need an HDR to achieve a good result. In this kind of shots it''s better to shoot during the blue hour after sunset when the equilibrium between light and darkness is perfect. Moreover here you could fix the distorsion of the buildings.', '2012-03-22 10:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
